SUMMARY:Make & Take: Mother & Daughter Flower Pot Workshop
DESCRIPTION:Take time to bond and make a beautiful hand-painted gift \nOn the day before Mother’s Day\, artist Debbie Sizemore\, of Dot & Dusty\, is offering a hands-on mandala dotting workshop to create a colorful flower pot for spring blooms. You (and your mother/daughter/bestie) will decorate a terra cotta pot in bright spring colors against a dark background. \nMandala dotting is the art of using dots of paint to create intricate circular patterns. No experience is necessary. Focusing on the beauty and symmetry of your design and creating artwork along with others can be a great way to relax\, leave stress behind. \nWalk-ins are welcome\, but reservations are recommended\, so call to save your seat today! Choose from four start times. The registration fee includes instruction on mandala dotting\, as well as a 4-inch terra cotta pot\, paint and other supplies. \n$25 per person or $40 for two people includes instruction and all materials for one painted pot each. \nDate: Saturday\, May 9 \nTimes:\n11 a.m.\n12 p.m.\n1 p.m.\n2 p.m. \nTo save your space: Call (717) 344-6875.
URL:https://bird-in-hand.com/event/make-take-mother-daughter-flower-pot-workshop/
LOCATION:Bird-in-Hand Artisan Village\, 2705 Old Philadelphia Pike\, Bird-in-Hand\, PA\, 17505\, United States
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://bird-in-hand.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/MothersDayPotMT.jpg
END:VEVENT
