UID:7442085f2ec4e86609c81b4046dc5f92@calendar.lancasterlibraries.org
DESCRIPTION:Community\, Adults\, Seniors\n\nIf you have a spare hour or tw
 o a week\, we invite you to join the “Little Library that Could” as we
  expand our reach and services in 2026 during Columbia’s 300th Anniversa
 ry. We are launching a Friends Group to take some of the pressure off our 
 dedicated staff. It’s a great way to make new friends\, share your inter
 ests with others\, and help the library expand its footprint in the commun
 ities we serve.If any of these planned projects grab your interest\, consi
 der joining them for their first meeting!Cataloging our collection Columbi
 a History ArtifactsAssembling themed displays at the Market HouseSuperchar
 ge Adult Game NightWork on Outdoor Landscaping and BeautificationResearch 
 and Write About Columbia HistoryBook Delivery to the Elderly and InfirmJum
 p-Start Special Interest Book ClubsVolunteer for Special Community Outreac
 h Projectsand more!Click HERE to register for the Friends Group Meeting!
LOCATION:Columbia
URL:https://calendar.lancasterlibraries.org/event/columbia-public-library-
 friends-group-meeting-174941
