X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Lancaster Libraries": "https://calendar.lancasterlibraries.org/event/virtual-reality-career-exploration-173757"}
X-SOURCE-ID:lancaster_libraries
SUMMARY:Virtual Reality Career Exploration
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260528T163000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260528T180000
UID:69d0b5f0aa9be37b0f9bc81cbdc4587a@calendar.lancasterlibraries.org
DESCRIPTION:Business & Career\, STEM\, Teens\, Adults\n\nJoin the Adamstow
 n Area Library and Goodwill for a Career Exploration Workshop which includ
 es exploring options for different career fields\, what qualities are impo
 rtant at work\, and conducting a self-assessment to match interests to car
 eers. The workshop starts at 4:30 PM and is free.This workshop also includ
 es the opportunity to conduct over 50 different jobs in an immersive hands
 -on Virtual Reality experience. It allows job seekers to experience work i
 n different careers and ultimately get on a path to a well-paying job. Sim
 ulations are about 10 minutes long. All are available in Spanish. The job 
 categories include agriculture\, architecture and construction\, finance\,
  health science\, hospitality and tourism\, human services\, information t
 echnology\, law and public safety\, manufacturing\, science and technology
 \, and transportation. Registration is required for this event. This progr
 am is for individuals aged 14-25.Your instructor is Lisa Ference\, who has
  a B.S. in Computer Science from Desales University. She is a retired FBI 
 Supervisory Special Agent who investigated computer crimes and intrusions 
 for the FBI in New York City. She now works at Goodwill Keystone Area\, pr
 oviding learning opportunities in the Lehigh Valley and surrounding counti
 es.
LOCATION:Adamstown\, ADM Community Room
URL:https://calendar.lancasterlibraries.org/event/virtual-reality-career-e
 xploration-173757
X-SOURCE:Lancaster Libraries
END:VEVENT
