X-SOURCE-ID:lancaster_libraries
SUMMARY:Creating a Bird Friendly Garden
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260622T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260622T190000
UID:77cc0254026eef0ae1bcd0b2a93ef1c5@calendar.lancasterlibraries.org
DESCRIPTION:Presentation\, Summer Reading\, Adults\n\nTurn your garden int
 o a haven for birds! See your landscape from a bird's eye view to discover
  how to create a vibrant habitat that provides the food\, water and shelte
 r that birds need to thrive. You'll explore how to get started with your o
 wn bird-friendly garden with practical tips like choosing appropriate nati
 ve plants and gardening practices that invite more birds to your garden\, 
 including songbirds and hummingbirds. No matter your space or experience l
 evel\, you can transform your garden into a safe and welcoming environment
  for your favorite birds and bird species in decline. Presented by Penn St
 ate Extension Master Gardener Colleen Emmerling. Ages 18+.
LOCATION:Ephrata\, EPH 1/2 Multipurpose Room Projector Side
URL:https://calendar.lancasterlibraries.org/event/creating-bird-friendly-g
 arden-166598
