BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Lancaster Libraries": "https://calendar.lancasterlibraries.org/event/teen-book-talk-156958"}
X-SOURCE-ID:lancaster_libraries
SUMMARY:Teen Book Talk: Shadow and Bone
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260622T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260622T190000
UID:18692badaf1d232a046fa86586735829@calendar.lancasterlibraries.org
DESCRIPTION:Book Club\, Teens\n\nFor Teens ages 13-18 years of age only.Ca
 lling all teen readers! Join us for Teen Book Talk\, a fun and engaging mo
 nthly book discussion group led by members of our Teen Advisory Board! Boo
 k selections are chosen by teens during advisory meetings. Interested in j
 oining the Teen Advisory Board? Sign up through the library calendar. Each
  month\, we’ll dive into a new title—ranging from trending young adult
  fiction to graphic novels\, fantasy epics\, thought-provoking contemporar
 y stories\, and more.This month\, we'll be reading "Shadow and Bone" by Le
 igh Bardugo.  Alina Starknov is orphaned by the Boarder Wars.  She is take
 n from obscurity and her only friend\, Mal\, to become the protege of the 
 mysterious Darkling\, who trains her to join the magical elite in the beli
 ef that she is the Sun Summoner\, who can destroy the monsters of the Fold
 . You’ll get the chance to share your thoughts\, hear different perspect
 ives\, and connect with fellow book lovers in a relaxed and welcoming spac
 e. Snacks will be provided\, and occasionally we’ll have themed activiti
 es or giveaways tied to the book!Note: To help everyone stay present and g
 et the most out of the experience\, we ask that all phones stay in pockets
  or bags during the program. Thank you for your cooperation!Library Progra
 m PoliciesNo Show – Patrons failing to cancel their registration for mor
 e than 2 library programs in a month will be restricted from registering f
 or future programs for a period of one month’s time. Please cancel your 
 registrations at least 2 hours prior to the start of the program to allow 
 for those on the waiting list to be notified of their change in registrati
 on status.Late Arrivals – Please arrive 10 minutes prior to the start of
  the program to allow for parking and other circumstances. The program wil
 l begin promptly at the designated time. At this time\, your spot will be 
 forfeited to those on the wait list who will be granted entry. If spots re
 main\, registrants may be allowed into the program. However\, registrants 
 will not be permitted to enter the program 5 minutes past the start time.C
 heck In - All participants must provide an emergency contact number upon r
 egistration or at the start of the program.
LOCATION:Manheim Township\, MTP Study Room #119
URL:https://calendar.lancasterlibraries.org/event/teen-book-talk-156958
X-SOURCE:Lancaster Libraries
END:VEVENT
