X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Lancaster Libraries": "https://calendar.lancasterlibraries.org/event/copy-understanding-immigration-law-naturalizationbecoming-citizen-160893"}
X-SOURCE-ID:lancaster_libraries
SUMMARY:Understanding Immigration Law: Asylum
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260627T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260627T123000
UID:0af9b149d54ae314b40825556e2bee5f@calendar.lancasterlibraries.org
DESCRIPTION:Discussion\, Presentation\, Adults\n\nRegistration is preferre
 d\; walk-ins will be accommodated as space allows. Best for adults and old
 er interested teens.We welcome local immigration attorney Paige Britton\, 
 who will share her professional experience working within the U.S. immigra
 tion system over several sessions\, exploring a different element each mon
 th.Asylum – How can a person gain safety from persecution?Learn about th
 e laws that offer protection to noncitizens fleeing harm in their home cou
 ntries. How easy is it to get asylum\, and who qualifies? What do they nee
 d to prove\, and how do they make their case for asylum relief? This event
  is offered solely as information about the American legal system and shou
 ld not be construed as legal advice. If you need legal counsel on this or 
 other immigration matters\, please consult a qualified immigration attorne
 y.
LOCATION:Quarryville\, QVL C.X. Carlson Cultural Room
URL:https://calendar.lancasterlibraries.org/event/copy-understanding-immig
 ration-law-naturalizationbecoming-citizen-160893
X-SOURCE:Lancaster Libraries
END:VEVENT
