X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Lancaster Libraries": "https://calendar.lancasterlibraries.org/event/dino-tales-172623"}
X-SOURCE-ID:lancaster_libraries
SUMMARY:Dino Tales - Preschool
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260706T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260706T110000
UID:6d9f4fd45a88cca91bae1f060e5f34e6@calendar.lancasterlibraries.org
DESCRIPTION:Community\, Discussion\, Presentation\, Storytime\, Summer Rea
 ding\, Toddlers\n\nAnimals that roam the earth today have special adaptati
 ons for survival. Dinosaurs thousands of years ago had their own adaptatio
 ns\, but theirs were bigger and bolder. Participants will learn about dino
 saur adaptations of the past by reading a book with the naturalist\, going
  on a dinosaur hunt\, making their own observations\, and creating their o
 wn dinosaurs with unique adaptations. Everyone will finish with a game of 
 pin the tail on the dinosaurs!
LOCATION:Manheim Community\, MAN Kreider Cultural Center
URL:https://calendar.lancasterlibraries.org/event/dino-tales-172623
X-SOURCE:Lancaster Libraries
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Lancaster Libraries": "https://calendar.lancasterlibraries.org/event/knitting-club-152066"}
X-SOURCE-ID:lancaster_libraries
SUMMARY:Knitting Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260706T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260706T120000
UID:0e58114ab70e158fbf749bb22e4e7ad4@calendar.lancasterlibraries.org
DESCRIPTION:Arts & Crafts\, Adults\, Seniors\n\nKnitting Club typically me
 ets the 1st and 3rd Monday of the month\, from 10 a.m. until noon and the 
 second and last Tuesday of each month from 6 p.m. – 7:30 p.m.  Knitting 
 Club is for people who knit and like to share the craft. This is not a cla
 ss or instruction\, just a friendly gathering to knit and work on projects
 . Must bring all your own supplies. Crocheters also welcome. No registrati
 on required.
LOCATION:Lititz\, LTZ Board Room
URL:https://calendar.lancasterlibraries.org/event/knitting-club-152066
X-SOURCE:Lancaster Libraries
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Lancaster Libraries": "https://calendar.lancasterlibraries.org/event/parachute-play-154573"}
X-SOURCE-ID:lancaster_libraries
SUMMARY:Parachute Play
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260706T101500
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260706T104500
UID:456e1a6fdc8721e5dd56a82017af41a1@calendar.lancasterlibraries.org
DESCRIPTION:Storytime\, Toddlers\, Children\n\nJoin us for a cooperative m
 ovement program where we will use our imaginations while we play with a pa
 rachute! Stories and songs will be incorporated\, while we move about and 
 use our motor skills. A great activity for young children and their adults
  to come together and share an exciting and engaging play experience! (Mus
 t be 18 months-younger 3 years old with an adult\, adult involvement is re
 quired)Adults attending with their child(ren) do NOT need to register. Ple
 ase add any additional registrants to your registration if more than one c
 hild that will be participating in the program.Registration will open at 9
 :00AM on Wednesday\, June 24th for Manheim Township and East Lampeter resi
 dents and on Friday\, June 26th for residents of other municipalities.Stor
 ytime PoliciesNo Show – Patrons failing to cancel their registration for
  more than 2 library programs in a month will be restricted from registeri
 ng for future programs for a period of one month’s time. Please cancel y
 our registrations at least 2 hours prior to the start of the program to al
 low for those on the waiting list to be notified of their change in regist
 ration status.Late Arrivals – Please arrive 10 minutes prior to the star
 t of the program to allow for parking and other circumstances. The program
  will begin promptly at the designated time. At this time\, your spot will
