BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Lancaster Libraries": "https://calendar.lancasterlibraries.org/event/teen-zine-160311"}
X-SOURCE-ID:lancaster_libraries
SUMMARY:Teen Summer Zine
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260711T123000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260711T140000
UID:676699d2d474d12b04740cf24569b1df@calendar.lancasterlibraries.org
DESCRIPTION:Summer Reading\, Teens\n\nThe Teen Summer Zine is back for 202
 6\, with a new lineup of mentor authors and artists\, new locations and a 
 celebration of the hand-made roots of zines! Students will learn from loca
 l arts professionals while creating their own hand-made publications that 
 can include comics\, fan art and fan fiction\, poetry\, collage and illust
 rations. All art and writing materials will be provided\, along with snack
 s! Students may submit their favorite pieces for publication into a county
 -wide digital zine that will be available for checkout through Libby at th
 e end of the summer. All Lancaster County teens are welcome to participate
 . Sessions will take place at the following times and locations: June 13\,
  1pm. Manheim Township Library: Create Comics with graphic novelist Jamar 
 Nicholas\; June 27\, 12:30pm\; Ephrata Public Library: Make a FanZine with
  Lancaster Zine Fest's Louise LoBello\; July 11\,12:30pm. Ephrata Public L
 ibrary: Create Collage Poetry with author and poet Lindsay Bandy\; July 25
 \, 1pm. Quarryville Library: Make Zine Art with local artist Ciana Malchio
 ne. To register\, please visit the appropriate library’s events calendar
 . Ages 12-19.
LOCATION:Ephrata\, EPH Conference Room
URL:https://calendar.lancasterlibraries.org/event/teen-zine-160311
X-SOURCE:Lancaster Libraries
END:VEVENT
