BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Lancaster Libraries": "https://calendar.lancasterlibraries.org/event/srp-parks-program-adultsall-ages-tbd-134998"}
X-SOURCE-ID:lancaster_libraries
SUMMARY:Archaeology in Lancaster County
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260716T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260716T190000
UID:abe4a33d73488f67dfbdd66e639dd956@calendar.lancasterlibraries.org
DESCRIPTION:STEM\, Summer Reading\, Children\, Tweens\, Teens\, Adults\, S
 eniors\n\nAdults and interested older children. Please register each perso
 n in your group.The land we today call Lancaster County has a rich history
  that stretches millennia into the past. Archaeology has given us a unique
  toolset to peer into this deep past and glimpse the lives of the earliest
  peoples to live on this land\, who have been hunting\, gardening\, engine
 ering\, philosophizing\, crafting\, dancing\, playing\, and much more for 
 countless generations. This presentation will focus on pre-European contac
 t and early contact archaeological sites and theories to paint a picture o
 f what life may have been like for some of the various Indigenous peoples 
 who inhabited and shaped this region in the past.
LOCATION:Quarryville\, QVL C.X. Carlson Cultural Room
URL:https://calendar.lancasterlibraries.org/event/srp-parks-program-adults
 all-ages-tbd-134998
X-SOURCE:Lancaster Libraries
END:VEVENT
