DESCRIPTION:STEM\, Children\n\nDid you know you can make some amazing colo
 rful designs by using some common foods\, common household items\, and a l
 ittle imagination? 🤔 It's chemistry done in a bright and imaginative wa
 y.  🎆🎇This program is for kids ages 6 - 9 years old. *Registration w
 ill open at 9:00AM on Wednesday\, July 1st for Manheim Township and East L
 ampeter residents and on Wednesday\, July 8th for residents of other munic
 ipalities.Library Program Policies No Show – Patrons failing to cancel
  their registration for more than 2 library programs in a month will be re
 stricted from registering for future programs for a period of one month’
 s time. Please cancel your registrations at least 2 hours prior to the sta
 rt of the program to allow those on the waiting list to be notified of the
 ir change in registration status. Late Arrivals – Please arrive 10 min
 utes prior to the start of the program to allow for parking and other 
 circumstances. The program will begin promptly at the designated time. At 
 this time\, your spot will be forfeited to those on the wait list who will
  be granted entry. If spots remain\, registrants may be allowed into the p
 rogram. However\, registrants will not be permitted to enter the progr
 am 5 minutes past the start time. Accompanying Adults – This program i
 s for adults and children to enjoy together. Please plan to attend and be 
 engaged with your child. Drop offs will not be permitted. Drop Off Program
  – This program is intended for children over the age of 6 years who c
 an participate independently. Adult(s) must be present to check in child w
 ith youth services staff prior to program. Adults will not be allowed in t
 he event space.  *For children ages 6–7\, this is a drop-off program
 \; however\, a parent or caregiver must remain nearby and wait outside t
 he program room for the duration of the program.
