UID:7952eb97bd167c2e2fdafb2652bc147a@calendar.lancasterlibraries.org
DESCRIPTION:Summer Reading\, Everyone\n\nGet ready for a wild prehistoric 
 adventure! Join us for an exciting\, family-friendly reptile show where th
 e creatures of today help us explore the dinosaurs of the past. We'll intr
 oduce you to lots of rescued reptiles—snakes\, lizards\, turtles and mor
 e—and discover how these modern animals are connected to the ancient gia
 nts that once roamed the Earth. Reptile expert and certified Class Clown J
 esse Rothacker will share fascinating facts\, fun stories and up-close enc
 ounters with incredible reptiles while explaining their connection to dino
 saurs. Kids and adults alike will have the chance to see these animals up 
 close and ask questions during this interactive experience. This engaging 
 program blends science\, discovery and a little prehistoric imagination! C
 ome explore the reptile world and uncover the living relatives of dinosaur
 s! All ages.
LOCATION:Ephrata\, EPH Multipurpose Room
